/api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/13f2ecc84bdf257af19b370a2f03a0f02d15674d","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/13f2ecc84bdf257af19b370a2f03a0f02d15674d","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/13f2ecc84bdf257af19b370a2f03a0f02d15674d/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0"}]},{"sha":"af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGFmNWRhYjViNzdmYjFmNzgyMWJkMTYwMjAzZWY3NWE5MmJhMjZkZDA","commit":{"author":{"name":"Nick Hollon","email":"nick.hollon@langchain.dev","date":"2026-06-01T17:20:32Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-06-01T17:20:32Z"},"message":"fix(sdk-py): percent-encode thread_id in v3 stream transport default paths (#7954)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes #7953.\n\nThe v3 SSE and WebSocket stream transports build their default paths by\ninterpolating `thread_id` directly into the URL:\n\n```python\nself._commands_url = commands_path or f\"/threads/{thread_id}/commands\"\nself._stream_url   = stream_path   or f\"/threads/{thread_id}/stream/events\"\n```\n\nThis skips the `_quote_path_param` escaping that the rest of the SDK\nadopted in #7893. A `thread_id` containing reserved characters or\ndot-segments is then normalized by the HTTP/WebSocket stack before\ntransmission. For example, `thread_id = \"../assistants/abc\"`:\n\n| | before |\n|---|---|\n| constructed | `/threads/../assistants/abc/commands` |\n| wire path | `/assistants/abc/commands` |\n\nSo the value stops being one opaque identifier under\n`/threads/{thread_id}/...` and silently hits a different resource.\n\n## Fix\n\nReuse the existing `_quote_path_param` helper for the **default** paths\nin all four transports (`http`, `sync_http`, `ws`, `sync_ws`). Explicit\n`commands_path` / `stream_path` overrides are left untouched, so callers\nthat pass their own paths opt out of encoding as before.\n\n`_quote_path_param(\"../assistants/abc\")` → `..%2Fassistants%2Fabc`,\nwhich the HTTP/WS stack no longer collapses.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds `tests/streaming/test_transport_path_encoding.py` covering all four\ntransports:\n- default `_commands_url` / `_stream_url` / `_stream_path` are\npercent-encoded,\n- the actual SSE wire path (async + sync) stays under `/threads/`,\n- the built WebSocket URL (async + sync) stays under `/threads/`,\n- explicit path overrides are left untouched.\n\n`make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` all pass in `libs/sdk-py`\n(491 passed).","tree":{"sha":"adddfeb6c5f102b1efd60b9dd338e15b05153a67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/adddfeb6c5f102b1efd60b9dd338e15b05153a67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqHb9gCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYXcQAIjU94xz5x3yxgwaa3NAau2R\nZHdA5ubGW8wtIuB+5jy9qzOOk8crXiDfpUfKuwCvY8w+wsTfTTXO4W44YZkhj/wx\nZtmwdZUEIR6NyTE0KNSok9gvbIUOmDmoqEkHRs442ravkdIZHZKT+1huWkkRe6uZ\n0klo70rmsXkMM0gquZRC1A05RUaw041de6mOuuEx+QYO6sOU/Fi8XXOqyUloE7PC\nle31ddtI1O+I5zefBDJswdxcawXT5Vj1xOozHs8HXsU9cIEMugN4014xPCLQ9Fok\nrOfHnmvx55m9InJGSFe12GSZ8ro4uUg6KOyf3snH9oVNLO2FY2V3Gcj+uhg3UFXO\np/jGFbHvMuXNEwlCZmXUnpWQDwSEmJkW9Vsl8+d9Cp6OxL/fM1m5KVQhMRQvGJeg\njosFm5YHbGK3srOLi1BoJ5OPSnBrF2+VYqSwKdsxD5kruz1P8NU1b2EqAHL3jj39\nEQaZLv06MnUfSM8Bms6ja5NyBKe2HAR9v+WyIT1W8h0ClOkWFACVAhx5ZwxnbKKl\nDCvwgxgJcsjGpescrshsc0mCmwgO3MCo4DAHTBRM2YBH2FJoxZjCWzWCQra6pWu4\noORSa1VA2LoKgjKJ2lERhnvN8wIF/UJkNWnF9tr/J8L5NcGEt3H8z1whtkDjTQ4i\nfRcRafrpwg7dU3NEq8YX\n=ZPnK\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree adddfeb6c5f102b1efd60b9dd338e15b05153a67\nparent 312c6d0ac1e0de338e7974a0d1f864eefab2dd2d\nauthor Nick Hollon <nick.hollon@langchain.dev> 1780334432 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780334432 -0400\n\nfix(sdk-py): percent-encode thread_id in v3 stream transport default paths (#7954)\n\n## Problem\n\nFixes #7953.\n\nThe v3 SSE and WebSocket stream transports build their default paths by\ninterpolating `thread_id` directly into the URL:\n\n```python\nself._commands_url = commands_path or f\"/threads/{thread_id}/commands\"\nself._stream_url   = stream_path   or f\"/threads/{thread_id}/stream/events\"\n```\n\nThis skips the `_quote_path_param` escaping that the rest of the SDK\nadopted in #7893. A `thread_id` containing reserved characters or\ndot-segments is then normalized by the HTTP/WebSocket stack before\ntransmission. For example, `thread_id = \"../assistants/abc\"`:\n\n| | before |\n|---|---|\n| constructed | `/threads/../assistants/abc/commands` |\n| wire path | `/assistants/abc/commands` |\n\nSo the value stops being one opaque identifier under\n`/threads/{thread_id}/...` and silently hits a different resource.\n\n## Fix\n\nReuse the existing `_quote_path_param` helper for the **default** paths\nin all four transports (`http`, `sync_http`, `ws`, `sync_ws`). Explicit\n`commands_path` / `stream_path` overrides are left untouched, so callers\nthat pass their own paths opt out of encoding as before.\n\n`_quote_path_param(\"../assistants/abc\")` → `..%2Fassistants%2Fabc`,\nwhich the HTTP/WS stack no longer collapses.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdds `tests/streaming/test_transport_path_encoding.py` covering all four\ntransports:\n- default `_commands_url` / `_stream_url` / `_stream_path` are\npercent-encoded,\n- the actual SSE wire path (async + sync) stays under `/threads/`,\n- the built WebSocket URL (async + sync) stays under `/threads/`,\n- explicit path overrides are left untouched.\n\n`make format`, `make lint`, and `make test` all pass in `libs/sdk-py`\n(491 passed).","verified_at":"2026-06-01T17:20:32Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/af5dab5b77fb1f7821bd160203ef75a92ba26dd0/comments","author":{"login":"nick-hollon-lc","id":274035459,"node_id":"U_kgDOEFVzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/274035459?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc","html_url":"https://github.com/nick-hollon-lc","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nick-hollon-lc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.co