ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb"}]},{"sha":"f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","node_id":"C_kwDOKFU0ldoAKGYyNWEwZjRmNGMzODllOWU2ZWQ2NmI5OThhMjM3NTY0MDRiN2ViZGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"syachamaneni-lc","email":"sreekara.yachamaneni@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-28T21:34:18Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T21:34:18Z"},"message":"fix(langgraph): [LSD-1507] Distinguish between user cancelled and other cancellations (#7920)\n\n- Distinguish between Node cancellations and other cancellations\n- Use python 3.11+ feature where `cancelling() == 0` when it is the node\ncancelling\n- Bubble up the node cancellation example so the client can take care of\nit instead of silently failing without reporting it.\n\nRead the full contributing guidelines:\nhttps://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/contributing/overview\n\n> **All contributions must be in English.** See the [language\npolicy](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/contributing/overview#language-policy).\n\nIf you paste a large clearly AI generated description here your PR may\nbe IGNORED or CLOSED!\n\nThank you for contributing to LangGraph! Follow these steps to have your\npull request considered as ready for review.\n\n1. PR title: Should follow the format: TYPE(SCOPE): DESCRIPTION\n\n    - feat(langgraph): add multi-tenant support\n- Allowed TYPE and SCOPE values:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/blob/main/.github/workflows/pr_lint.yml#L19-L43\n\n2. PR description:\n\n  - Write 1-2 sentences summarizing the change.\n- The `Fixes #xx` line at the top is **required** for external\ncontributions — update the issue number and keep the keyword. This links\nyour PR to the approved issue and auto-closes it on merge.\n  - If there are any breaking changes, please clearly describe them.\n- If this PR depends on another PR being merged first, please include\n\"Depends on #PR_NUMBER\" in the description.\n\n3. Run `make format`, `make lint` and `make test` from the root of the\npackage(s) you've modified.\n\n  - We will not consider a PR unless these three are passing in CI.\n\n4. How did you verify your code works?\n- Existing unit tests pass\n- New unit tests added\n- Used langgraph deployment to make sure the feature is working as\nexpected.\n\nAdditional guidelines:\n\n- All external PRs must link to an issue or discussion where a solution\nhas been approved by a maintainer, and you must be assigned to that\nissue. PRs without prior approval will be closed.\n- PRs should not touch more than one package unless absolutely\nnecessary.\n- Do not update the `uv.lock` files or add dependencies to\n`pyproject.toml` files (even optional ones) unless you have explicit\npermission to do so by a maintainer.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\n<!-- If you'd like a shoutout on release, add your socials below -->\nTwitter: @\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/","tree":{"sha":"3c864a2db302e4ee22c3b5a58a9e8f6d46d33690","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/trees/3c864a2db302e4ee22c3b5a58a9e8f6d46d33690"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/git/commits/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGLTaCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAoewQACNLZIcZvejuuIRYCi2A/csD\nbM3csoI4+1nSzAOqE3TASWMudY8D1O/1iqYfQwx/PPfNKmqS/znHq4mlT3pY5uGG\n01BeuKGmXgbs9mfOqq7KbIZA6t2OmIwTSfEYh977LUcNIO7Ds7Ql1puTOWXWkiuq\nJf1io2krBdxJY0LY36Qozy4fdxT+hOo3yQQedzSFUX0zaF3liTd5SnoGl+2dw8wu\nIA2j5xrrXPhpun+SBuxVgXdCddrC3aH9WlXb19zIqTusfOhS3HnNQBltJz3yrYFJ\nEZ1xBDfuBqGkugFvunNkLNbiWY6yJEccjb4rdNkVrFIghLHOwEafZKcNuyXE1OzX\nWn70SjWkEDUNAQlQPYzFxKLq3+qaz5cJNQuUNtTwVBmuWN8d3oba7RfUpLxgcCux\nk2NlxT9nsZJbtEqoAgyYySvV8/pcC01hf7Jc9nCMG0S2gNrJFS+EAcLgcVp1+ijq\nUVjG03Bk94aEr48FPdjs49zOxtvFm9t4VVnjuz71W8eNOlk51IVCr7cFhsynOZfZ\n1/zjlwe/CwFgITuT2F/dftIpt7njBHoRnXbtNYmcblN1w39RNhHGb164VYTWtdYb\n8acKc74BtZVhnyndfsFh2SF54Gd1iDiylCnRKBgyOaB2ZexsYZLnelMFKs+MMdx4\n6ZdOpEcxG0koryelyvvP\n=MKZW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 3c864a2db302e4ee22c3b5a58a9e8f6d46d33690\nparent ea4aa79a60dcd824d288da0a359f774956e7e8c2\nauthor syachamaneni-lc <sreekara.yachamaneni@langchain.dev> 1780004058 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780004058 -0700\n\nfix(langgraph): [LSD-1507] Distinguish between user cancelled and other cancellations (#7920)\n\n- Distinguish between Node cancellations and other cancellations\n- Use python 3.11+ feature where `cancelling() == 0` when it is the node\ncancelling\n- Bubble up the node cancellation example so the client can take care of\nit instead of silently failing without reporting it.\n\nRead the full contributing guidelines:\nhttps://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/contributing/overview\n\n> **All contributions must be in English.** See the [language\npolicy](https://docs.langchain.com/oss/python/contributing/overview#language-policy).\n\nIf you paste a large clearly AI generated description here your PR may\nbe IGNORED or CLOSED!\n\nThank you for contributing to LangGraph! Follow these steps to have your\npull request considered as ready for review.\n\n1. PR title: Should follow the format: TYPE(SCOPE): DESCRIPTION\n\n    - feat(langgraph): add multi-tenant support\n- Allowed TYPE and SCOPE values:\nhttps://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/blob/main/.github/workflows/pr_lint.yml#L19-L43\n\n2. PR description:\n\n  - Write 1-2 sentences summarizing the change.\n- The `Fixes #xx` line at the top is **required** for external\ncontributions — update the issue number and keep the keyword. This links\nyour PR to the approved issue and auto-closes it on merge.\n  - If there are any breaking changes, please clearly describe them.\n- If this PR depends on another PR being merged first, please include\n\"Depends on #PR_NUMBER\" in the description.\n\n3. Run `make format`, `make lint` and `make test` from the root of the\npackage(s) you've modified.\n\n  - We will not consider a PR unless these three are passing in CI.\n\n4. How did you verify your code works?\n- Existing unit tests pass\n- New unit tests added\n- Used langgraph deployment to make sure the feature is working as\nexpected.\n\nAdditional guidelines:\n\n- All external PRs must link to an issue or discussion where a solution\nhas been approved by a maintainer, and you must be assigned to that\nissue. PRs without prior approval will be closed.\n- PRs should not touch more than one package unless absolutely\nnecessary.\n- Do not update the `uv.lock` files or add dependencies to\n`pyproject.toml` files (even optional ones) unless you have explicit\npermission to do so by a maintainer.\n\n## Social handles (optional)\n<!-- If you'd like a shoutout on release, add your socials below -->\nTwitter: @\nLinkedIn: https://linkedin.com/in/","verified_at":"2026-05-28T21:34:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/commit/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/langgraph/commits/f25a0f4f4c389e9e6ed66b998a23756404b7ebdb/com